//! task: write
//! ask: Show the difference between `firma` and `mutabilis` bindings.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4
//! explain: `firma` ("firm") binds a value that cannot be reassigned; assigning to it is EXS-E0306. `mutabilis` binds a variable that can. The type annotation is optional where the initializer determines it. A binding declared without an initializer is not zero-filled, and reading it before assignment is EXS-E0307.

publica functio exemplum() -> u32 {
    firma a: u32 = 40;
    mutabilis b: u32 = 1;
    b = b + 1;
    redde a + b;
}
